ices, and you are solely responsible for payment of any third-party fees.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.3. You acknowledge and agree that all applicable fees are collected as part of each Transaction, either by the relevant smart contracts or by a transfer instruction that the Pump Platform includes in the Transaction you sign (including, in the case of the Platform Fee, a transfer to a Wallet designated by the Pump Entities or to the Referral Vault of a Referrer under Section 4.9), and you authorise the deduction of those fees from the Digital Assets used in that Transaction. Any other sum that you owe to us under these Terms is payable on demand.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.4. <strong>Amending our fees: </strong>We may adjust our fees, and introduce new fees, from time to time by updating the Fees Page. A change to our fees takes effect when the amended Fees Page is published or on any later date stated on the Fees Page, and Section 14.1 does not require advance notice of it. If you do not wish to accept the changed fees, you must cease use of the Pump Platform and relevant Pump Services. Your continued access to or use of the Pump Platform and relevant Pump Services shall be deemed acceptance of the updated fee.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.5. <strong>Calculations: </strong>Any calculations of fees made by the Pump Entities or affiliates in connection with your use of the Pump Services are final and binding on you in the absence of Manifest Error.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.6. <strong>Creator Fees and Cashback Coins</strong></p><p class="text-white dark">Certain tokens launched by users of the Pump Platform may include “Creator Fees”. Creator Fees are fees which are collected by the protocol for each transaction and paid to the creator of the token (except as set forth herein). The Pump Entities make no representations or warranties regarding the Creator Fees to you or any token creator.</p><p class="text-white dark">Creator Fees are dependent on network conditions, smart contracts, and third-party infrastructure. The Pump Entities do not guarantee that Creator Fees will be successfully charged or distributed for any particular transaction. We are not liable for on-chain failures, network congestion, or other technical issues that may prevent fee collection or payout.</p><p class="text-white dark">Where possible, the Pump Platform will display an estimated breakdown of Creator Fees, protocol fees, the Platform Fee and any other relevant fees prior to transaction confirmation. However, the actual fee applied and charged is determined by the underlying smart contracts and may differ slightly from the displayed estimate, for example due to slippage, network conditions, or rounding.</p><p class="text-white dark">Creator Fees are routed to one or more designated wallet addresses as configured by the token creator, or as otherwise specified by the applicable smart contract. In some configurations, Creator Fees may be shared among multiple wallets.</p><p class="text-white dark">The Pump Entities do not control how Creator Fees are ultimately used, distributed, or shared between creators, team members, promoters, referrers, or other third parties. Any such arrangements are strictly between you and those third parties.</p><p class="text-white dark">You are solely responsible for determining and fulfilling any tax obligations related to Creator Fees or other activity using the Pump Platform, including reporting and remitting income, capital gains, VAT, or similar taxes. The Pump Entities and their affiliates do not provide tax advice in any jurisdiction for any purposes.</p><p class="text-white dark">You agree that you will use Creator Fees in compliance with all applicable laws and regulations (including securities, commodities, AML, and KYC requirements, as applicable), not use Creator Fees to launder money, finance terrorism, or engage in fraud or other illegal activities and not misrepresent Creator Fee settings, token economics, or related rights to others.</p><p class="text-white dark">If you make any public statements or marketing materials about tokens using the Creator Fees, you must ensure those statements are accurate and not misleading.</p><p class="text-white dark">Some Creator Fees may be subject to a community takeover (“CTO”). A CTO occurs when control over Creator Fees and certain admin rights are handed from the original deployer to a new community‑chosen team or individual. CTOs are handled in the sole discretion of the Pump Entities and their affiliates or designees. CTOs may be governed by separate terms, as stated in the CTO application.</p><p class="text-white dark">The Pump Entities waive all liability, except as explicitly stated herein, for any actions taken with respect to a CTO. By accepting Creator Fees, you acknowledge that those Creator Fees are subject to the CTO process and may be re-routed through the CTO process.</p><p class="text-white dark">The Pump Platform may support a special launch mode for certain tokens (“Cashback Coins”). In this mode, a portion or all of the fees that would otherwise be allocated as Creator Fees are instead redirected as “Cashback Rewards” to eligible users of the token.</p><p class="text-white dark">A token launched as a Cashback Coin cannot subsequently be converted by its creator into a token that pays standard Creator Fees, but may be converted into a Holder Rewards Coin through a CTO, in which case Section 4.8 applies to it from the time of conversion. You acknowledge that by choosing cashback mode at launch, the original creator may permanently forgo some or all creator‑fee revenue that would otherwise be payable to the token creator or related Wallets.</p><p class="text-white dark">Cashback Rewards are funded from on‑chain fees generated by transactions in the relevant Cashback Coin, in such proportion and under such conditions as are encoded in the smart contracts. If there is no activity or insufficient fee generation, no Cashback Rewards will accrue. The timing, mechanics, and amounts of Cashback Rewards are determined by code and may depend on variables outside the control of the Pump Entities, such as network congestion, validator behavior, and third‑party protocol integrations. Rewards may fail to accrue or be distributed in some cases, and there is no guarantee of any minimum or ongoing reward.</p><p class="text-white dark">Cashback Coins do not guarantee any minimum or fixed rate of return, yield, income, recovery of fees, trading costs, or the value of any tokens or assets.</p><p class="text-white dark">The present availability of Cashback Rewards does not guarantee the future availability or level of Cashback Rewards.</p><p class="text-white dark">Cashback Rewards are not interest, dividends, or any other form of guaranteed payment. They are conditional, discretionary, and dependent on network and protocol behavior. You should not treat Cashback Rewards as predictable or assured income.</p><p class="text-white dark">You are solely responsible for determining the tax treatment of any Cashback Rewards you receive (or are deemed to receive) and for complying with all applicable tax reporting and payment obligations. Cashback Coins and Cashback Rewards may be subject to securities, commodities, or other regulatory frameworks in one or more jurisdictions. We do not provide legal, tax, or investment advice, and do not represent that any Cashback Coin or Cashback Reward is compliant with any particular regulatory regime.</p><p class="text-white dark">If you are a token creator, admin, promoter, or otherwise have an economic interest in a Cashback Coin (including any share of Cashback Rewards that may be routed to you or your affiliates), you may be subject to additional disclosure or transparency obligations under applicable law.</p><p class="text-white dark">You agree that you will not misrepresent the existence, rate, or reliability of any Cashback Rewards, the relationship between Cashback Rewards and token price, liquidity, or risk, or any personal financial interest you have in the relevant Cashback Coin.</p><p class="text-white dark">We are not a party to, and do not police, your disclosures to your users, followers, or investors. You remain solely responsible for compliance with all applicable laws and regulations in connection with such communications.</p><p class="text-white dark">Cashback mode is no longer available for new launches. Existing Cashback Coins continue to operate solely on the basis of the underlying smart contracts: Cashback Rewards continue to accrue on Transactions that are submitted using instructions that support cashback, and are not credited (the fee being paid to the creator instead) where a trading interface submits a Transaction without them; accrued Cashback Rewards remain claimable until claimed, although we may modify, suspend, or discontinue support for Cashback Coins at any time, including by ceasing to provide a user interface or by retiring the instructions through which they trade. Where a Cashback Coin is converted into a Holder Rewards Coin, Cashback Rewards cease to accrue from the conversion and Cashback Rewards already earned remain claimable.</p><p class="text-white dark">In cases of critical bugs, exploits, or other security incidents affecting Cashback Coins, we may take emergency measures where technically feasible (for example, disabling certain front‑end actions or prominently warning users). Such measures do not guarantee the security or recoverability of any assets or rewards.</p><p class="text-white dark">We have no obligation to upgrade, patch, migrate, or otherwise maintain any smart contracts associated with Cashback Coins, except where explicitly stated.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.7 <strong>EVM Transactions. </strong>You may initiate Transactions on EVM Blockchains using the Pump Platform. A fee is collected by the Pump Platform as part of each such Transaction at the rate set out on the Fees Page. The general purpose of these fees is to pay gas and transaction costs on the EVM Blockchain on which the transaction occurs, however, we do not separately track or account for the actual transaction costs for EVM Blockchain transactions. These fees are configurable by the Pump Platform and are subject to change. The Platform Fee described in Section 4.9 applies to Transactions on EVM Blockchains submitted through the Pump Platform in addition to the fees described in this Section 4.7 and to any fees charged by the third-party bridge, swap provider or network used to execute them.</p><p class="text-white dark">4.8 <strong>Holder Rewards.</strong></p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(a) <strong>Holder Rewards Coins. </strong>The Pump Platform may allow the creator of a User-Generated Digital Asset to enable, at launch, a holder rewards mode for that token (a “Holder Rewards Coin”). Where holder rewards mode is enabled, the fees that would otherwise be allocated as Creator Fees on Transactions in that token are instead allocated for distribution to Wallets that hold the token (“Holder Rewards”), at the rate displayed on the Pump Platform at launch and encoded in the applicable smart contracts. The holder rewards election is permanent: a Holder Rewards Coin cannot be converted into a token that pays Creator Fees to any person, and the recipient of its fees cannot be changed, by the creator, through a CTO, or otherwise. The rate may be changed only through a CTO and only where the Pump Platform permits a creator-set rate for that token (see Section 4.6 and the Fees Page). A token that was not launched as a Holder Rewards Coin (including a Cashback Coin) may be converted into a Holder Rewards Coin only through a CTO; the conversion is irreversible, Creator Fees accrued before the conversion are paid to the then creator (or, where Creator Fees were shared under a sharing configuration, transferred to the Holder Rewards vault), and only fees on Transactions after the conversion are allocated to Holder Rewards. You acknowledge that by choosing holder rewards mode at launch, the original creator permanently forgoes the Creator Fee revenue that would otherwise be payable to the token creator or related Wallets.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(b) <strong>Programmatic operation. </strong>Holder Rewards are funded solely from on-chain fees generated by Transactions in the relevant Holder Rewards Coin, which accumulate in a program-controlled vault for that token. The accrual, calculation, and distribution of Holder Rewards are carried out by the smart contracts and automated systems of the Pump Platform (together, the “Holder Rewards Program”) in accordance with the parameters published on the Pump Platform or in our public documentation from time to time and encoded in the Holder Rewards Program, which include the minimum holding required to be eligible for a distribution (expressed as a value in U.S. dollars and converted into a token amount by reference to a price quote obtained at the time of each distribution round), how and when holdings are measured (including by taking more than one snapshot and using the lower balance), which addresses are counted or excluded as holders (for example, bonding curves, liquidity pools, program-controlled addresses, and addresses controlled by a Pump Entity), minimum vault balances before a round is run, the maximum number of eligible holders for which a round will be run, rounding conventions, and distribution frequency (the “Holder Rewards Parameters”). No Pump Entity calculates, reviews, or approves individual distributions, and no Pump Entity exercises discretion over the amount of Holder Rewards, if any, distributed to any particular Wallet. If there is no trading activity or insufficient fee generation, no Holder Rewards will accrue. Holder Rewards are collected and, where distributed, paid in the Supported Pair Asset or Secondary Pair Asset with which the Holder Rewards Coin is paired (or such other Digital Asset as the Holder Rewards Parameters specify), and their value may fluctuate with that asset. Holder Rewards are allocated among eligible Wallets pro rata to their eligible holdings at the time of the distribution round; the length of time for which a token has been held is not a factor.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(c) <strong>Programmatic distribution. </strong>Where the conditions encoded in the Holder Rewards Program are met, Holder Rewards are distributed automatically by airdrop to the Wallets that the Holder Rewards Program identifies as holding the Holder Rewards Coin at the relevant time, without any claim, request, or other action by you. Whether a Wallet is treated as holding a Holder Rewards Coin, in what amount, and at what time, is determined solely by the Holder Rewards Program by reference to on-chain data, and the output of the Holder Rewards Program is final and binding on you in the absence of Manifest Error. The Holder Rewards Program depends on third-party RPC providers, indexers, price feeds, and Supported Networks that are not controlled by the Pump Entities, and distributions may be delayed, fail, or be calculated incorrectly as a result. A distribution round is run for a Holder Rewards Coin only when the Holder Rewards Parameters are satisfied; in particular, no round is run while the vault balance is below the minimum, while the number of eligible holders exceeds the maximum we set, or while no reliable price quote for the token is available, and a Holder Rewards Coin that has not traded for the period set in the Holder Rewards Parameters may cease to be monitored until it trades again, in each case with fees continuing to accumulate in the vault. We may change the Holder Rewards Parameters for new launches at any time, and may change the Holder Rewards Parameters for existing Holder Rewards Coins where technically feasible and where we consider it necessary to address a bug, exploit, security incident, legal or regulatory requirement, or Manifest Error.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(d) <strong>Reserved right not to distribute. </strong>NOTWITHSTANDING THE PROGRAMMATIC OPERATION OF THE HOLDER REWARDS PROGRAM, THE PUMP ENTITIES RESERVE THE RIGHT, IN THEIR SOLE AND ABSOLUTE DISCRETION, TO PAUSE, SUSPEND, DISABLE, DELAY, REDUCE, WITHHOLD, OR CANCEL THE HOLDER REWARDS PROGRAM OR ANY DISTRIBUTION OF HOLDER REWARDS, IN WHOLE OR IN PART AND IN RESPECT OF ANY OR ALL HOLDER REWARDS COINS OR WALLETS, AT ANY TIME, FOR ANY REASON OR FOR NO REASON, WITHOUT NOTICE AND WITHOUT LIABILITY TO YOU OR ANY OTHER PERSON. Holding a Holder Rewards Coin does not create any entitlement, right, claim, or expectation to receive Holder Rewards, and no Holder Rewards are owed to, earned by, or vested in you unless and until they are actually delivered to your Wallet by the Holder Rewards Program. Fees in a Holder Rewards vault may be paid out only by the Holder Rewards Program under the control of a distribution authority held by the Pump Entities; they are not held for your benefit or on your behalf, and until delivered they are not your property. Fees allocated to Holder Rewards that are not distributed in a round, for whatever reason (including rounding, ineligibility, deferral, or the exclusion of a Wallet), remain in the vault and are carried forward to later rounds, and may instead be applied to the costs of operating the Holder Rewards Program, retained by the Pump Entities, or otherwise applied as we determine in our sole discretion. No Pump Entity has any obligation to sweep, return, or pay out any vault balance.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(e)<!-- --> <strong>Sanctions and anti-money laundering screening. </strong>WITHOUT LIMITING SECTION 4.8(d), WE MAY SUBJECT ANY WALLET TO SANCTIONS, ANTI-MONEY LAUNDERING, AND RELATED COMPLIANCE SCREENING BEFORE, AS PART OF, OR AFTER ANY DISTRIBUTION OF HOLDER REWARDS, AND MAY CAUSE THE HOLDER REWARDS PROGRAM TO EXCLUDE FROM ANY OR ALL DISTRIBUTIONS ANY WALLET THAT DOES NOT PASS THAT SCREENING OR THAT WE DETERMINE OR REASONABLY SUSPECT FALLS WITHIN ANY OF THE FOLLOWING. Screening may be carried out using automated screening tools, on-chain analytics, and third-party screening providers. Without limitation, a Wallet may be excluded where it is, or where the screening tools we use indicate that it is: (i) owned or controlled by, or acting on behalf of, a person or entity that is the subject of sanctions administered by the U.S. Office of Foreign Assets Control, the United Kingdom, the European Union, the United Nations, or any other Regulatory Authority, or that is owned or controlled by such a person or entity; (ii) located in, resident in, or associated with a Prohibited Jurisdiction or a jurisdiction described in Section 21(p); (iii) associated with a mixing or tumbling service, a darknet marketplace, ransomware, hacks, exploits, stolen funds, fraud, or other illicit activity; or (iv) otherwise flagged by the screening tools or providers we use. You must not hold a Holder Rewards Coin, or receive Holder Rewards, if you are a person described in (i) or (ii), and you represent each time Holder Rewards are delivered to your Wallet that you are not such a person and are not receiving them for the benefit of such a person. Any Holder Rewards that would otherwise have been attributable to an excluded Wallet are forfeited and will not be paid at a later date. We are not required to notify you that your Wallet has been excluded, to disclose the basis for that determination, or to reconsider it, and exclusion determinations are final and binding on you. We are not liable for any error, delay, or omission in screening, including any false positive or any failure to screen. By holding a Holder Rewards Coin you consent to the screening of your Wallet, including the sharing of your Wallet address and related on-chain and transaction data with screening providers, in accordance with our Privacy Notice.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(f) <strong>Other exclusions. </strong>We may also cause the Holder Rewards Program to exclude any Wallet from any distribution of Holder Rewards where the Wallet, or a person we reasonably believe controls it, has engaged in Prohibited Use, has breached these Terms, is or has been subject to termination, suspension, or restriction under Section 15, has used multiple Wallets or otherwise structured holdings or Transactions in order to obtain Holder Rewards, or where we reasonably suspect any Improper Intent or Manifest Error in connection with the relevant Holder Rewards Coin.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(g) <strong>No guarantee; not income. </strong>Holder Rewards Coins do not guarantee any minimum or fixed rate of return, yield, income, distribution, recovery of fees or trading costs, or the value of any tokens or assets. The present availability of Holder Rewards does not guarantee the future availability or level of Holder Rewards. Holder Rewards are not interest, dividends, profit share, revenue share, or any other form of guaranteed or periodic payment. They are conditional and dependent on trading activity in the Holder Rewards Coin, the Holder Rewards Parameters, the correct operation of the Holder Rewards Program and the infrastructure on which it relies, network and protocol behaviour, and the rights reserved in Sections 4.8(d) to 4.8(f). The amount of Holder Rewards you receive, if any, will depend on factors including the volume of Transactions in the Holder Rewards Coin, your balance relative to other eligible holders at the relevant time, the Holder Rewards Parameters, and rounding, and may be zero. You should not acquire or hold a Holder Rewards Coin in the expectation of receiving Holder Rewards or treat Holder Rewards as predictable or assured income.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(h) <strong>Airdrop mechanics and errors. </strong>Distributions of Holder Rewards are on-chain transactions and may fail, be delayed, or be irreversible once submitted. The Holder Rewards Program is software and may contain bugs, errors, or vulnerabilities. The Pump Entities are not responsible for Holder Rewards sent to a Wallet that you no longer control, that cannot receive the relevant Digital Asset, or that was compromised, or for any Holder Rewards lost or misdirected as a result of a bug or exploit in the Holder Rewards Program, a blockchain reorganisation or similar network event, or the failure of any Supported Network, RPC provider, indexer, or other infrastructure. Where Holder Rewards are distributed in error, in an incorrect amount, or to a Wallet that should not have received them, the Pump Entities may, but are not obligated to, pause the Holder Rewards Program and correct the error, and you agree to return any Holder Rewards received in error on request and authorise us to set off any over-distributed amount in accordance with Section 29.13. Before Holder Rewards are allocated in a distribution round, an amount is reserved from the vault to meet the network, rent, priority-fee and other costs of that round, up to the per-eligible-holder amount stated on the Fees Page; the costs actually incurred are reimbursed from the vault to a Wallet controlled by the Pump Entities, any unused reserve remains in the vault for later rounds, and any shortfall is borne by the Pump Entities. The amount of Holder Rewards you receive is therefore net of those costs.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(i) <strong>Taxes and information requests. </strong>You are solely responsible for determining the tax treatment of any Holder Rewards you receive (or are deemed to receive) and for complying with all applicable tax reporting and payment obligations. Where required or permitted by Applicable Law, we may withhold amounts from, report, or condition any distribution of Holder Rewards on your providing identifying, tax, or other information, and we may cause the Holder Rewards Program to exclude any Wallet whose owner has not provided information we have requested.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(j) <strong>Regulatory status. </strong>Holder Rewards Coins and Holder Rewards may be subject to securities, commodities, or other regulatory frameworks in one or more jurisdictions. We do not provide legal, tax, or investment advice, and do not represent that any Holder Rewards Coin or Holder Rewards are compliant with any particular regulatory regime or lawful to acquire, hold, or receive in your jurisdiction. If you are a token creator, admin, promoter, or otherwise have an economic interest in a Holder Rewards Coin, you may be subject to additional disclosure or transparency obligations under Applicable Law. You agree that you will not represent, in any public statement, marketing material, or communication, that Holder Rewards are guaranteed, fixed, periodic, or assured, misrepresent the existence, rate, reliability, or source of any Holder Rewards or the relationship between Holder Rewards and token price, liquidity, or risk, or fail to disclose any personal financial interest you have in the relevant Holder Rewards Coin. We are not a party to, and do not police, your disclosures to your users, followers, or investors.</p><p class="text-white dark pl-6">(k) <strong>Changes and discontinuance. </strong>We may, at our discretion, modify, suspend, or discontinue holder rewards mode for new launches, and may modify, suspend, or discontinue the Holder Rewards Program for any or all existing Holder Rewards Coins, at any time and without notice. Existing Holder Rewards Coins may continue to trade solely on the basis of the underlying smart contracts, even if the Holder Rewards Program ceases to operate or the Pump Entities cease to provide a user interface, and the Holder Rewards Program may continue to run for a Holder Rewards Coin that has been removed, hidden, or restricted on the Pump Platform for as long as it is traded on-chain, unless we pause